UID: WORK-SEMANTIC-CONFLICT-TRACKING
TITLE: Track semantic rules before a DSL exists
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Track semantics before a DSL exists. The operator cannot track semantics
today or know when conflicts come up; until they can craft a DSL, the LLM is
the semantic layer. Wanted: a way to record a semantic rule when it is
stated (a temp semantic node?) so conflicts surface instead of living in
session memory.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Verbatim, since the shape is undecided: "temp semantic node? until I can
craft a DSL and you're my semantic layer until then. i can't track semantics
right now, know when conflicts come up."
<<<
